course: dictionary
lesson: 4567
title: Paying heed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To heed something means to pay attention to it and do what it says. A warning or a piece of advice can be heeded. Heed is a formal word, so you will meet it most in old stories, fables and safety signs.
explain: «Heed the warning signs» tells you to notice the signs and act on them. The word heed is a clue to whether a character listened to good advice or ignored it.
explain: Look for the phrases: «take heed», «pay heed to», and «pay no heed». «The Rat paid no heed to his doleful self-reproaches» means the Rat did not pay attention to his own sad blaming of himself. When you are not sure, swap in «paid attention to» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Heed (verb) means to pay attention to advice or a warning and do what it says.
fact: Heed (noun) means attention: «take heed» means pay attention, and «pay no heed» means ignore.
fact: The verb forms are heeds, heeded and heeding: «She heeded the warning and turned back.»
fact: Heed is formal or old-fashioned, so look for it in stories, fables and safety messages.
fact: «Ere» means before, and «irrevocable» means something that can never be taken back.
exercise: «Heed the warning signs» tells you to... | Count them | Ignore them | *Pay attention to them and act on them | Take them home
exercise: «The Rat paid no heed to his doleful self-reproaches.» What does paid no heed mean? | Felt sorry for himself | Listened very carefully and wrote it down | *Did not pay attention to | Paid lots of money
exercise: Which word means pay attention to advice and do what it says? | Ignore | *Heed | Ere | Doleful
test: Mum says, «Take heed of the bridge sign.» What does she want you to do? | Count the cars | Paint the sign | Ignore the sign | *Notice the sign and act on it
test: «The knight heeded the wise old owl and turned back.» What did the knight do? | He ignored the owl and went on | *He listened to the advice and turned back | He fell asleep | He flew away
exam: «He paid no heed to the warning and walked onto the thin ice.» What does paid no heed mean? | Read the warning aloud | *Did not pay attention to the warning | Bought some ice | Asked for a second warning
